{"slug": "fusilli-with-basil-mint-spinach-and-ricotta-sauce", "nyt_id": 7287, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/7287-fusilli-with-basil-mint-spinach-and-ricotta-sauce", "name": "Fusilli With Basil, Mint, Spinach and Ricotta Sauce", "author": "Molly O’Neill", "description": "", "servings": {"text": "4 servings", "min": 4, "max": 4, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 15, "raw": {"total": "15 minutes"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 pound fusilli pasta", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "lb", "item": "fusilli pasta", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "1 cup lightly packed basil leaves", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "lightly packed basil leaves", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "¾ cup lightly packed mint leaves", "group": null, "quantity": 0.75, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "lightly packed mint leaves", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "½ cup well-drained, chopped frozen spinach (thawed) or blanched fresh spinach leaves", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "well-drained", "preparation": "chopped frozen spinach (thawed) or blanched fresh spinach leaves", "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "½ cup finely grated Parmesan cheese", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "finely grated parmesan cheese", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "2 tablespoons unsalted butter, softened", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "unsalted butter", "preparation": "softened", "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "2 cloves minced garlic", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "clove", "item": "minced garlic", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "1 ¼ teaspoons kosher salt", "group": null, "quantity": 1.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "kosher salt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "½ teaspoon freshly ground black pepper, plus more for serving", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "freshly ground black pepper", "preparation": "plus more for serving", "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "¾ cup ricotta cheese", "group": null, "quantity": 0.75, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "ricotta cheese", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "3 strips crisp-cooked bacon, crumbled (optional)", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "strip", "item": "crisp-cooked bacon", "preparation": "crumbled", "optional": true}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Bring a large pot of salted water to a boil and cook the pasta according to package directions. Meanwhile, combine the basil, mint, spinach, Parmesan, butter, garlic, salt and pepper in the bowl of a food processor and process until fairly smooth. Add the ricotta and pulse until combined. When the pasta is tender, drain, reserving 1 tablespoon of the water it cooked in. Transfer the hot pasta to a bowl and toss with the herb-and-ricotta mixture and the reserved tablespoon of cooking water. Sprinkle the pasta with the bacon and serve immediately with freshly ground black pepper on the side."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 712.4, "protein_g": 28.9, "carbohydrates_g": 91.1, "fat_g": 25.1, "saturated_fat_g": 12.4, "trans_fat_g": 0.2, "cholesterol_mg": 65.0, "sodium_mg": 548.8, "fiber_g": 5.1, "sugar_g": 3.3, "unsaturated_fat_g": 10.5, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": [], "diet": [], "course": ["main course"], "meal": ["dinner"], "occasion": [], "other": ["basil", "boil", "pasta", "pastas", "ricotta", "weeknight"]}, "images": [], "rating": {"ave